    "retrieval": [
      {
        "heading": "Appoint independent help and define document questions",
        "text": "Local help is most useful when roles are clear. Before appointing someone, ask whom they represent, who pays them, whether they receive referral compensation, what conflicts may arise and what their written scope excludes. A helpful introduction does not settle those questions."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Appoint independent help and define document questions",
        "text": "Agree how questions will be handled across time zones and in which language important conclusions will be delivered. Specify who receives reports and who may instruct additional paid work. Distinguish acknowledgement of a message from approval to act, so a hurried reply from one participant is not mistaken for a family decision."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Agree the family decision and use plan",
        "text": "A shared family intention needs a shared operating plan. \u201cWe will all use it\u201d leaves open who pays, who decides, who books popular dates and who deals with problems. Discuss these matters while the choice is still open, rather than after one person has become attached to a particular apartment."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Complete a family-purpose worksheet",
        "text": "Keep ownership questions distinct from informal expectations. Tell counsel who would contribute money, who would be registered, who expects to use the property and what should happen if circumstances change. Ask for advice on documenting the chosen arrangement rather than assuming an internal spreadsheet settles legal rights."
      }
    ],
